   APPENDIX B: Source Availability Option.

      This Appendix forms part of the License for Option Files, as
      defined in subsection (a) of this Appendix. It does not apply to
      any other file.

      (a) Option Files. "Option Files" shall mean (i) files of the Work
          that carry the notice set out in subsection (f) of this
          Appendix, and (ii) Derivative Works of those files, including
          any new file that contains material copied or adapted from an
          Option File.

      (b) Precedence. For Option Files, this Appendix overrides Section
          4(f) and the Whole-Work Exception in Section 4(o) to the
          extent they conflict with it. In all other respects, the
          License applies to Option Files unchanged.

      (c) Source Availability. If You distribute an Option File in
          Object form, You must make its Source form available to every
          recipient of the Object form, under this License, except
          material described in Section 4(k), which remains under the
          terms under which You received it, by one of the following
          means:

          (i)   accompanying the Object form with the Source form; or

          (ii)  informing recipients, with the Object form, how they may
                obtain the Source form promptly and for a charge no more
                than the reasonable cost of distribution, and keeping
                the Source form so available for at least three (3)
                years after Your last distribution of that Object form.

          The period of three (3) years under paragraph (ii) applies
          separately to each individual or Legal Entity that
          distributes an Option File in Object form, and runs from that
          individual's or Legal Entity's own last distribution of that
          Object form. Any individual or Legal Entity that receives an
          Option File in Object form and distributes it further has the
          same obligation under this subsection, for the same period of
          three (3) years. The expiry of the period that applies to one
          individual or Legal Entity does not end or shorten the period
          that applies to any other. You may not satisfy this
          subsection by relying on another person's offer under
          paragraph (ii).

          You may choose the terms that apply to the Object form,
          provided that those terms comply with this subsection and do
          not limit or alter the rights that recipients have in the
          Source form under this License.

      (d) Notice. Only the Licensor may first apply the notice set out
          in subsection (f) of this Appendix to a file of the Work. Once
          applied, that notice must not be removed from that file or
          from any Derivative Work of it, except that it may instead be
          given in another manner permitted by Section 4(c). Every
          Derivative Work of an Option File, including any new file
          described in subsection (a)(ii) of this Appendix, must carry
          that notice, or be accompanied by it in a manner permitted by
          Section 4(c), and adding it to such a Derivative Work is not a
          first application of it.

      (e) Larger Works. This Appendix applies only to Option Files, and
          not to any other file in a Larger Work. If You use the
          Whole-Work Exception for a work that includes an Option File,
          the whole of that work shall be treated as an Option File.

      (f) How to Apply. To apply the Source Availability Option to a
          file, add the following notice below the notice set out in
          Appendix A:

              This file is subject to Appendix B (Source Availability
              Option) of the File-Level Copyleft License (FLCL),
              Version 1.0. If you distribute this file, or a Derivative
              Work of it, in Object form, you must make its Source form
              available as Appendix B requires.

          Where the notice cannot reasonably be included in a file, for
          example because of the file's format, the notice may instead
          be given in a separate plain text file, of any name,
          distributed with the Work or the Derivative Work. That file
          must set out the notice and clearly identify each file to
          which it applies, for example by name or path. In that file,
          the words "this file" in the notice refer to each file so
          identified. Each file so identified shall be treated as
          carrying the notice, and that separate notice file, and the
          identification of each file in it, shall be subject to
          subsection (d) of this Appendix as if it were the notice in
          each identified file.
